<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Simon August, Count of Lippe-Detmold</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1727–1782</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Simon August (1727–1782) was Count of Lippe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/detmold">Detmold</a> from 1734, succeeding as a child. An enlightened ruler, he reformed schools, poor relief and agriculture and improved the administration of his small Westphalian county. His son Leopold I accepted the princely title in 1789, turning the county into the Principality of Lippe.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/simon-august-count-of-lippe-detmold.jpg" alt="Simon August, Count of Lippe-Detmold" width="320" height="375" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Simon_August_Graf_zur_Lippe_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
